E-BARD extends BARD: G. Giudici, A. Maurino and P. Zuccolotto, "BARD: A
Basketball Action Recognition Dataset for multi-label classification",
Computer Vision and Image Understanding 267 (2026) 104713,
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cviu.2026.104713.

FFmpeg is fetched at build time by scripts/fetch_ffmpeg.py rather than kept
in this repository. The builds used are LGPL-2.1-or-later, or GPL-2.0-or-later
where they include GPL-licensed components; the exact terms ship with the
binary in the installer.

Ollama is fetched at build time by scripts/fetch_ollama.py rather than kept in
this repository, and ships unmodified. Its MIT licence travels with it in the
installer as README-OLLAMA.txt.

The language models Ollama runs are NOT bundled. The app downloads the one it
needs on first launch, and each carries its own licence — Gemma, for example,
is covered by the Gemma Terms of Use rather than by anything here. That is
also why they are downloaded rather than shipped: redistributing them would
mean accepting those terms on every user's behalf.


